WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:33.140
[ Music ]

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:47.980
[Narrator:] Oil is where you find it. And the search for  oil is never-ending, constant. It spans the globe, 
coating a lake in Venezuela, a desert in Arabia,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:55.060
a Louisiana bayou, or rugged barely-explored Northern 
Canada.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.411
And you take oil where you find it,

00:00:58.411 --> 00:01:03.744
hard to live in, hard to breathe in, hard to work in, land.

00:01:03.744 --> 00:01:16.000
The people of the lands differ.  Language, customs, 
traditions vary. Neither oil nor the oil-seeker can alter a 
culture overnight, yet oil brings change.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:27.411
This is Talara, Peru and so is this.  National customs, 
when treated with respect and dignity, prove no barrier 
to an oil company's operation.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:38.411
Socially, culturally, man is supremely adaptable. And 
physically, there is no great difference between the 
American, the Venezuelan,

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:44.360
the Peruvian, the Finn, or the Arabian.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:51.660
The crux of the problem is adapting the physically unchanged human being to a physically changed world.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:02:00.711
This all-important problem--fitting the worker to his 
industrial environment--is a prime concern to the 
medical department of Jersey Standard.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.720
Here at 30 Rockefeller Plaza, headquarters of a 
worldwide organization of affiliated companies,

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.520
one of the most advanced industrial health programs is focused.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:22.980
[Man 1:]  All company medical activities are based upon one theory, simply this:  A healthy employee is a happy employee.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:33.211
And a happy employee who knows his medical 
limitations and who is assigned to a job in keeping with 
his abilities to perform is an efficient employee.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:42.500
To assist in the health maintenance of the employee calls for a new interpretation of medicine as applied to  the needs of industry.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:49.080
We think of it as a positive program, as an act of cooperation with the employee

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:53.280
in maintaining his capacity for a rewarding, healthy life

00:02:53.280 --> 00:03:00.440
rather than waiting behind a desk, waiting for something to happen to the employee before we do anything.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:08.780
More and more, the doctor in industry will spend his  time keeping the fit fit, rather than trying to make the  unfit fit.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:17.578
Yes, industry is rapidly changing the environment of man, but man is having trouble adapting 
himself satisfactorily.

00:03:17.578 --> 00:03:23.844
Let's face it, many of these new industrial 
developments have created new medical  problems

00:03:23.844 --> 00:03:29.800
like air pollution, water pollution, high-altitude flying, and 
many others.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.378
That is why this field of medicine in industry is no longer confined to the plant.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:44.440
Now we are concerned with medical problems 
involving all employed individuals.

00:03:48.844 --> 00:03:57.178
The activities of the doctor in industry are in the neutral 
zone  between management and labor. His activities 
are tremendously varied and numerous.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:06.380
In this industry certainly, with over 500 different occupations, with the health of so many thousands of personnel to consider,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.800
the vast distances between installations adds to the complications.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.200
To handle this  task then, new techniques are needed,

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:23.880
with coordination of thought and action among all those who are interested in employee welfare is most essential.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:31.340
We doctors in industry must develop a program 
applicable to large installations and small ones, too.

00:04:31.344 --> 00:04:36.477
Our aim is to give the same sort of service as we have 
here at the central office.

00:04:36.478 --> 00:04:44.444
[Narrator:]  To the employees in, say, Hamburg, or Rio  de Janeiro, or in New Jersey,

00:04:44.444 --> 00:04:50.810
and in places where employees are isolated, they must 
have medical supervision, too.

00:04:50.811 --> 00:05:04.411
[ Music ]

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:11.080
[Man 1:]  Wherever the employee is, the facilities, the care, and the attitudes of those attending him must be tops.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:15.740
And wherever the employee is, the standard of medical supervision must be the same.

00:05:15.744 --> 00:05:25.510
This, of course, takes planning in a big, total way.  In  our view, four types of medical practice make up this 
total medical program.

00:05:25.511 --> 00:05:27.644
We'd like to tell you about it.

00:05:27.644 --> 00:05:40.900
Jersey's four-part program: preventive medicine, 
constructive medicine, educative medicine, and 
curative medicine.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:54.000
Now let us examine these, one by one, starting first 
with preventive medicine.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:02.700
[Narrator:] The success of preventive medicine is  often reflected in a graph, a sliding downward graph.

00:06:02.711 --> 00:06:11.177
In Venezuela, for example, malaria had always been a 
scourge, killing and maiming thousands every year.

00:06:11.178 --> 00:06:19.811
Now the disease has been eradicated by a positive program of action, worked out by management on the basis of guidance by the doctor in charge.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.080
Mosquito-breeding areas were 
made target number one.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:33.980
[ Music ]

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:38.511
Those who became victims of the disease 
were given immediate, efficient, thorough treatment.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:50.060
But the overall emphasis was on prevention rather  than cure. And this emphasis paid off in ways far more 
important than lines on a graph can show.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.120
So successful was the company's anti-
malarial  campaign

00:06:53.120 --> 00:07:00.480
that in Caripito Hospital, bed space formerly allotted  to malarial cases has been converted to doctors' offices.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:07.560
In Aruba, the major problem was amoebic dysentery.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.800
For years, the disease had been endemic in the area.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:21.480
In 1936, the health unit of the company began a  concerted attack on amoebic dysentery.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:30.880
New sanitary  techniques in the preparation of food were installed and carefully supervised. A boil or open sore can do a lot of  damage.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:36.760
Preventive measures, some simple, some more complicated, but the results were dramatic.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.720
[Music]

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:45.580
Frequency rate of disease dropped sharply.  Amoebic dysentery was virtually wiped out.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:52.340
The result, healthier, happier employees in Aruba.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:58.800
[ Music ]

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:07.900
In New York, a company employee bound for the Near East visits the health center for immunization shots that will protect him from the diseases

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:14.040
prevalent in his destination.  Preventive medicine, getting it before it gets you.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:25.640
[ Music ]

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:35.400
Periodically, health officers from affiliates located in all  corners of the globe meet in New York to discuss new approaches to old problems...

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:41.244
new problems constantly arising.  Their reports are carefully recorded.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:49.860
Out of these discussions, this exchange of 
information, come the dynamics of a modern practical  program for disease prevention.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:09:00.111
To implement the program, the industrial physician works closely with a skilled, efficient team.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:10.980
The industrial hygienist can answer key questions on  employee working conditions, location of jobs, 
materials handled.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:25.740
The chemist has an important contribution. So has the toxicologist, the nurse, the epidemiologist, the biostatistician, the safety engineer,

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:34.760
all of them with heavy responsibilities in the overcoming of industrial problems. But let's see what  happens when this team goes into action.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:44.620
1942, the  year the first commercial unit for fluid catalytic cracking was put into operation by a Jersey Standard affiliate.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:53.420
A heavy fraction from this process contains a  hydrocarbon, which under certain conditions, has been found to cause cancer in humans.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:10:00.900
Question, "Was this  heavy fraction a potential cancer hazard?" The answer 
had to be found.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:06.440
Representatives of the health unit and management met. The go-ahead was given.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:15.240
Cooperation of outstanding research institutes was asked and given. Experimental animals were painted with oil samples.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:22.320
This investigation and others demonstrated that certain of these heavy fractions,

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:26.380
under specific conditions caused cancerous growths on animals.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:32.460
Conclusion:  A cancer hazard existed where workers came in contact with these oils.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:39.500
More information was needed.  How many men were in contact with these oils? To what degree?

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:48.060
At company laboratories, a full-scale attempt was made to eliminate or diminish the possible disease-causing chemical compounds in the oil.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:54.220
Employees exposed to the possible disease-causing oils were examined every three months,

00:10:54.260 --> 00:11:00.240
and special attention was paid to warts, tumors, and other abnormalities of the skin.

00:11:00.244 --> 00:11:09.844
In the refinery, lines, tanks and other pieces of 
equipment containing the possibly disease-producing 
oil were painted orange for identification.

00:11:09.844 --> 00:11:16.140
Employees were instructed to remove oil from the skin  immediately by thorough washing with soap and water.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:20.160
[Music]

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:27.020
Protective clothing was provided and required on all jobs where there was possible contact with these oils.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:35.460
As a result of these and other precautions, there have been no cases of skin cancer among  workers since this program was established.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:44.378
A potential health problem had been found, investigated, and eliminated by the applications of the techniques of preventive medicine.

00:11:44.378 --> 00:11:49.144
[ Music ]

00:11:49.144 --> 00:11:55.000
[Speaker 1:]  Planned action in advance, that is the core of preventive medicine.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:12:05.400
We know too often in large-scale medical work the emphasis is all upon disease while little attention is paid to the individual as a total person.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:12.180
Constructive medicine, the second of a four-part program of constructive health maintenance,

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:21.720
tries to avoid this defect. Its major concern is the health of the whole man by adding life to years.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:31.500
Constructive medicine utilizes every facility and judgment at a doctor's disposal, so that he can detect disease early enough

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:37.880
to do something simple and positive about it at a price that the employee can afford to pay.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:47.540
In industry, the cornerstone of constructive medicine is in the concept of the complete health inventory medical examination.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:55.911
[Narrator:] The inventory medical examination is a total evaluation of the individual's health.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:03.144
This employee has been with the company for 15 years.  He is now taking his eighth periodic physical.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:11.900
The examination includes a psychological evaluation of  the individual.  How about the job?  Is he up to it?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:19.340
If he isn't, not only the job will suffer, but more important, the man's health will begin to break down.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:25.020
Thus, psychologically and physically, the total medical inventory is evaluated.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:33.280
The examinations are voluntary.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:43.800
No employee is forced to take them, and for those who 
do, the examination results are confidential, strictly 
between the employee and the physician.

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:59.840
Days later, physician and employee discuss the 
findings.  Advice is given for correcting existing defects 
and, if necessary, a private physician is recommended.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:13.240
Whether for the executive at a desk or 
a man in the field, constructive medicine helps the 
employee understand his capacity for achievement.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:18.500
It is imperative for every individual to know what his  health potential is.

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:22.680
That's why all employees, wherever 
they are, whatever their job,

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:27.400
are encouraged to visit the health center whenever they want to.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:33.660
Today, through any one of the many health centers of Jersey or its affiliates,

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:38.880
employees come for periodic physical inventories, willingly, gladly.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:56.680
At times, an employee will come in with a health problem that worries her deeply,  affects her work, her enjoyment of living.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:15:01.960
A complete inventory will help get to the root of the trouble, which at times is minor,

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:08.220
sometimes could be serious if not 
attended to.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:14.860
But it is attended to. The examination is thorough. The facts are obtained.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:19.940
And arrangements are made to forward her complete  medical file to the physician of her choice.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:33.680
If hospitalization is required, the cost will be covered by 
her health insurance. And the company will see to it 
that she suffers no loss of pay.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:38.111
[Music]

00:15:38.111 --> 00:15:46.211
Ten days later, the employee comes back to the 
company health center for a checkup. The problem 
was not dodged.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:54.740
It was met and resolved early so that the employee 
can now lead a happier, fuller life, the end purpose of 
constructive medicine.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:16:21.640
[Dance music ]

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:31.880
Not all the time is the story a pleasant one.  At times, 
an employee will report to the health unit with a specific 
complaint.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:42.540
Her profile revealed she had not reported at regular intervals for a periodic checkup.

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:50.700
The receptionist makes arrangements for the woman 
to receive a complete physical examination.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:17:02.440
The examination reveals a serious condition which 
should've been checked long before.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:11.520
Immediate hospitalization is suggested, but though everything

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:17.480
possible will be done for her, the probability is that the 
corrective action will be too late.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:35.178
[Speaker 1:] There is only one answer to the tragedy of a person who dies because of medical action called for too late. That is education.

00:17:35.178 --> 00:17:44.478
The spreading of accurate information about the  constructive, positive approach of modern medicine as applied to the medical needs of industry.

00:17:44.478 --> 00:17:54.011
When the employee understands that the idea of going  to a doctor only when you feel sick is as extinct as the 
hoop skirt...

00:17:54.011 --> 00:18:05.944
when the concept of the medical inventory is  thoroughly grasped by medical men as well as laymen, only then the benefits will be felt by everybody.

00:18:05.944 --> 00:18:12.944
That is the reason behind the third phase of a modern 
constructive health maintenance program for industry.

00:18:12.944 --> 00:18:23.600
This phase can be described as educative medicine. First of all, it involves extensive training of doctors, nurses, and other medical personnel

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:27.600
within Jersey Standard and its affiliated companies.

00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:40.578
[Narrator:]  To the home headquarters each year come company doctors from all over the world. It is a give-and-take relationship, a free discussion of problems,

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:46.580
an exchange of information among doctors who have  specialized in medicine as applied to the needs of industry.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:19:00.778
Forums are conducted on specific medical problems 
of industry, as here, the problems of alcoholism.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:12.340
The individual doctors observe, and later on their comments will be asked for, their frank comments, 
because educative medicine is a two-way street.

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:16.578
[Music]

00:19:16.578 --> 00:19:26.811
Often, it is not possible or practical for the doctors and 
nurses of every affiliate to visit the home headquarters. 
So, the home headquarters will visit the affiliate.

00:19:26.811 --> 00:19:31.944
[ Music ]

00:19:31.944 --> 00:19:37.244
Mutual problems are discussed. The on-the-spot 
situation is reviewed.

00:19:37.244 --> 00:19:42.477
Everywhere within the organization of affiliated 
companies, as here in Venezuela,

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:49.380
the training of nurses is never neglected, for a 
competent staff of nurses and technicians is a must.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:20:01.240
Medical students, the doctors of tomorrow, are invited  at company expense for a program of discussion, 
meetings, and visits to various facilities.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:22.220
Public and private health agencies are continually made aware of the work of the health units.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:34.080
Under the educative phase of the program, employees 
come to understand their physical makeup and their 
limitations.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:42.520
The employee suddenly stricken with stomach cramps 
will pass up the home remedy, and if the condition 
continues, he will check it with a doctor.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:54.060
The wife of an employee who suffers a heart attack 
knows immediately what to do: Stay put and call a 
doctor.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:21:01.960
It is in instances like these that educative medicine 
proves its worth.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:18.011
[Speaker 1:] The fourth phase of a modern constructive health maintenance program for industry is one which 
is very often over emphasized, the curative phase.

00:21:18.011 --> 00:21:27.811
All too often, clinical facilities have been set up by 
companies for the sole purpose of taking care of a 
medical emergency after it occurs.

00:21:27.811 --> 00:21:38.977
This is unfair, not only to the employee but to the 
company concerned as well.  It is strictly a case of 
locking the barn door after the horse has been stolen.

00:21:38.978 --> 00:21:46.944
But this is not to say that medicine as applied to the  needs of modern industry should ignore the best facilities and procedures available

00:21:46.944 --> 00:21:52.900
to deal with accidents and emergencies as they occur. Far from it.

00:21:54.144 --> 00:21:59.240
[ Music ]

00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:01.240
[Narrator:]  This is an emergency.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:59.011
[ Music ]

00:22:59.011 --> 00:23:02.811
Back at the health unit, the man's leg is x-rayed.

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:07.800
Emergency care is given to ease the pain, to start the 
healing process on its way.

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:17.300
The employee has a badly sprained ankle.

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:27.500
The patient's personal physician is notified and 
arrangements are made for hospitalization in 
accordance with his wishes.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:36.978
Once the elementary curative care is started, the 
burden of care must fall on the individual employee,

00:23:36.978 --> 00:23:41.611
who receives a full report to turn over to his own private 
physician.

00:23:41.611 --> 00:23:48.311
Good health is not a gift.  It is a personal responsibility 
which must be worked for.

00:23:48.311 --> 00:23:56.677
The employee has help in this search for good health.
He has the help of management, a progressive 
management which has set up a positive,

00:23:56.680 --> 00:24:05.680
vigorous medical program with adequate facilities and personnel at every installation to carry out the four-part program for better health:

00:24:08.580 --> 00:24:17.320
preventive medicine, constructive medicine, educative 
medicine, curative medicine.

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:18.640
[Music]

00:24:18.644 --> 00:24:27.410
Today, medical teamwork, intelligent planning, are helping the worker to achieve better health and a happier life.

00:24:27.411 --> 00:24:37.211
The employee gains. Management gains. This, then, is the reward of a positive program for industrial health.

00:24:37.220 --> 00:25:17.980
[ Music ]

